  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 506.05 Specific Procedures",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 506.05 Specific Procedures.\n\n(a) The start-up procedures required by Env-Dw 506.04(a)(1) shall include the following:\n\n(1) Inspecting all components of the distribution system including sanitary protective area(s), well(s), source meter(s), pump house(s), pump(s), treatment facility(ies), storage facility(ies), valve(s), blow-off(s), hydrant(s), backflow prevention device(s), if any, and sampling tap(s);\n\n(2) Disinfecting and flushing all distribution lines;\n\n(3) Correcting any current or previously-noted sanitary defects;\n\n(4) Submitting to the department proof of all outstanding public notice(s) from the previous season;\n\n(5) Submitting to the department any outstanding assessment reports from the previous season;\n\n(6) Submitting to a state-accredited laboratory all outstanding chemical and bacterial make-up sample(s); and\n\n(7) Resolving all outstanding violations or requirements.\n\n(b) The owner may include additional steps in the start-up procedures, such as sampling.\n\nSource. #10771, eff 2-1-15; ss by #14342, eff 8-22-25, EXPIRES: 8-22-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw500.html"
}
